---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="For school and college ceramics departments"
	description="Wheel booking between classes, kiln queues for a whole department and course rosters for school and college ceramics programs with one or two kilns."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">For schools &amp; colleges</p>
				<h1>A ceramics department that runs on the timetable, not the clipboard.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					One or two kilns, a semester of courses and a room full of students who want a wheel in
					the hour between lectures. Kilnbook keeps the wheels, the kiln shelf and the class lists in
					one place.
				</p>
				<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
			</div>
			<img
				src="/images/wheel-grid.svg"
				alt="A day view of four wheels booked in one-hour blocks from 9am to 6pm"
				width="480"
				height="300"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Wheels booked between classes</h2>
		<p>
			Students reserve wheels, hand-building tables and the slab roller in one-hour blocks from
			their phone, so the free hour between classes is spent throwing, not waiting. Set how many
			hours each group gets and how far ahead they can book, and freed-up slots appear on the
			calendar as soon as someone cancels. <a href="/features/wheel-time">More on wheel time</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>One kiln queue for the whole department</h2>
		<p>
			Students log a piece when they set it on the bisque shelf, and it goes into the right load for
			the right kiln. Staff can see how full each bisque, cone 6 and cone 10 load is, and every
			student with work in a load gets a text when it is unloaded. Each kiln keeps a firing log with
			the date, cone, schedule and who loaded it. <a href="/features/firings">More on firings</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Courses that follow the semester</h2>
		<p>
			Set up each course as a fixed series, like Wheel 101 on Tuesdays for the term, with drop-in
			sessions alongside it. Instructors get their own login with today's roster, can mark
			attendance from the studio tablet and leave notes for the next instructor.
			<a href="/features/classes">More on classes</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Which plan fits a department?</h2>
		<p>
			Most school programs fit the Studio plan, which covers up to 3 kilns with unlimited members,
			wheel and table reservations, and pickup texts when pieces come out of the kiln. A program
			with a single kiln can start on Starter, and departments on more than one campus can use
			Collective. <a href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Questions departments ask</h2>
		<div class="faq">
			<details>
				<summary>Is there a discount for school ceramics programs?</summary>
				<p>
					Yes. Registered nonprofits and school ceramics programs get 30% off any plan. Mention it
					when you book a demo.
				</p>
			</details>
			<details>
				<summary>We have two kilns. Which plan do we need?</summary>
				<p>
					The Starter plan covers one kiln, so two kilns means the Studio plan, which covers up to 3.
					If you add a fourth, you can move to Collective at any point in the month.
				</p>
			</details>
			<details>
				<summary>Can we import our students from a spreadsheet?</summary>
				<p>
					Yes. Upload a CSV with names and emails at the start of term, and we map the columns for
					you during setup.
				</p>
			</details>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>See it with your timetable.</h2>
			<p>Tell us about your kilns, your courses and your wheel room, and we will show you how Kilnbook fits.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
